# Build context for Dockerfile (CrystalOS backend image).
#
# The build stage compiles the shell, so src/, scripts/, public/ and the
# Vite/tsconfig files MUST stay in the context — excluding them was what made
# the previous Dockerfile fail at `COPY src` / at `npm run build`.

# Installed and rebuilt inside the image; shipping the host's copies only
# risks copying the wrong platform's binaries.
node_modules
dist

# VCS and host metadata.
.git
.gitignore
.gitmodules
.agents
.kilo
.freebuff

# Runtime data. The account database and the VPN session files live on a
# volume at /data (see the Dockerfile), and the image must never carry a copy
# of a real database or a dev server's log.
server/accounts/data
server/vpn/data
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.log
vite-dev.log

# Material the image does not read at build or run time. integrations/ is
# half-excluded: the build imports integrations/sndgames-remastered (the Games
# catalogue), while integrations/scramjet is a read-only submodule clone of the
# whole upstream repo that nothing imports — and a host that does not init
# submodules has no copy of it to exclude in the first place.
docs
integrations/scramjet
popup-blocker-master
reverse-engineer-anything
tmp-review
netlify.toml
RILL-WALKTHROUGH.md
